Name: EXAMPLE_SIMPLEANALYSIS
Summary: Example of using the SimpleAnalysis interface
Status: VALIDATED
Reentrant: true
Authors:
 - Andy Buckley <andy.buckley@glasgow.ac.uk>
Description:
  An example demonstrating how to use the simplified analysis interface,
  which provides default object definitions and reconstruction-level
  smearing without the user needing to explicitly set up projections.
  This should be particularly useful for reducing barriers to BSM-search
  analysis preservation, in which the fine detail of object definitions is
  not crucial.
Keywords: ['bsm', 'reco']
